                <pb facs="0954" n="842" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg842"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 892.001/4.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Siamese Minister to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Siamese Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Gloucester,
                                Mass.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-10-24"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October 24,
                    1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In deepest grief I beg to inform you that to the irreparable loss to my country
                    His Majesty the King of Siam, my august sovereign, passed away yesterday morning
                    at 12.45.</p>
                <p>I also have the honor to announce to you that His Royal Highness the Crown Prince
                    has duly succeeded to the crown and has been proclaimed King Maha
                    Vajiravudh.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Akharaj
                    Varadhara.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
